cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Afterstring Reachability, cycle 1: the Fail-Close Runtime Governor. A preregistered test whose setup failed before any counted run"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sham
    given-names: Paddy
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-13
repository-code: "https://github.com/IAmPaddySham/afterstring-reachability-governor-c1"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A preregistered reachability test of a new implementation of the Fail-Close Runtime
  Governor, with 90 sealed cases and bars frozen before any data. The counted run never
  took place: the cases were sealed before the policy and the governed actor existed as
  data, and the only available sources for the Governor's deny response and transition
  value were the graded expected outcomes, which would have made it pass by construction.
  No label was printed. The Governor code is described but not included: it was built and
  unit-tested but never run on the sealed cases, and will be released with a later cycle.
  Writing and records are CC BY 4.0 (see NOTICE).
keywords:
  - reachability
  - runtime governor
  - fail-closed
  - preregistration
  - evaluation design
